      "message": "1. For commands returning small, fixed attributes (GET_INFO with 6 u32s, GET_RAM_SIZE with 1 u32), passing 0 uses the default NLMSG_DEFAULT_SIZE (~4 KB page buffer), which easily holds the response.\n    2. For READ, the returned APF RAM buffer is dynamic and may exceed 4 KB, so nla_total_size(len) is passed to ensure the skb allocation is large enough to prevent -EMSGSIZE on large reads.",
