      "writtenOn": "2026-08-26T06:43:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Look deeper, it seems the morden gennetlink have the following logic to reject the non expected attribute\n\n  ### 1. Generic Netlink selects NL_VALIDATE_STRICT by default\n\n  In genetlink.c:931-946:\n\n        enum netlink_validation validate \u003d ops-\u003evalidate \u0026 no_strict_flag ?\n                           NL_VALIDATE_LIBERAL :\n                           NL_VALIDATE_STRICT;\n    ...\n        err \u003d __nlmsg_parse(nlh, hdrlen, attrbuf, ops-\u003emaxattr, ops-\u003epolicy,\n                    validate, extack);\n\n  ### 2. NL_VALIDATE_STRICT defines NL_VALIDATE_UNSPEC\n\n  In netlink.h:529-533:\n\n    #define NL_VALIDATE_STRICT (NL_VALIDATE_TRAILING |\\\n                    NL_VALIDATE_MAXTYPE |\\\n                    NL_VALIDATE_UNSPEC |\\\n                    NL_VALIDATE_STRICT_ATTRS |\\\n                    NL_VALIDATE_NESTED)\n\n  ### 3. Netlink parser validates each attribute against policy\n\n  In nlattr.c:634-640:\n\n            if (policy) {\n                int err \u003d validate_nla(nla, maxtype, policy,\n                               validate, extack, depth);\n\n                if (err \u003c 0)\n                    return err;\n            }\n\n  ### 4. Unspecified attributes (pt-\u003etype \u003d\u003d 0 / NLA_UNSPEC) are rejected\n\n  In nlattr.c:549-554:\n\n        case NLA_UNSPEC:\n            if (validate \u0026 NL_VALIDATE_UNSPEC) {\n                NL_SET_ERR_MSG_ATTR(extack, nla,\n                            \"Unsupported attribute\");\n                return -EINVAL;\n            }\n\n  Any attribute index omitted from a policy table has .type \u003d 0 (NLA_UNSPEC). When NL_VALIDATE_UNSPEC is active (part of NL_VALIDATE_STRICT), the parser aborts immediately with -EINVAL and sets the extack message \"Unsupported attribute\".",
      "parentUuid": "24f88777_2feae06a",
